  "slug": "diary-jess-waiting-mode",
  "tiktok": {
    "caption": "ADHD mom waiting mode is real: my toddler napped for 2 hours and i didn't start anything 🫠\n\nit's not laziness. when the kids are home part of your brain stays on alert for the next interruption, so starting feels impossible. what helped: one tiny first step, not the whole task.\n\ndo you get waiting mode too? 👇\nsave this for the next nap 📌\n\nthe app on the last slides is FOCO, link in bio 💜",
    "hashtags": [
      "#adhdmom",
      "#waitingmode",
      "#taskparalysis",
      "#adhdtiktok"
    ]
  },
  "instagram": {
    "caption": "ADHD mom diary: my toddler napped for 2 hours and I didn't start anything. It's called waiting mode.\n\nIt's not laziness. Part of my brain stays on alert for the next interruption, so I can't start.\n\n1. 1:00, nap starts, proposal due tomorrow\n2. I sit down to start... and wait\n3. 2:40, still nothing, now I'm mad at myself too\n4. I said the task out loud and did only step 1: open the doc\n\n2:58, first page done. She woke up at 3:05.\n\nSave this for the next nap, and send it to the mom friend who gets it.\n\n💜 The app I use is FOCO, link in bio.",
    "hashtags": [
      "#adhdmom",
      "#waitingmode",
      "#taskparalysis",
      "#adhdwomen"
    ],
    "altText": "Scrapbook-style diary carousel of a mom working from home during her toddler's nap: taped photos of her laptop, baby monitor and paperwork, cut-out photos of her with hand-drawn arrows, about ADHD waiting mode and starting a work task with one tiny step in FOCO."
